{"at":"2026-10-13T12:47:37.682Z","tool":"submit_plan","args":"{\"issue\":99001,\"plan\":\"# Text properties\\ncreate TC-1: \\\"Underline\\\" toggle: underlining a text and removing the underline\\ncreate TC-2: \\\"Underline\\\" toggle: where it is shown and hidden\\ncreate TC-3: Ctrl+U / Cmd+U on a selected or edited text\\ncreate TC-4: Ctrl+U with nothing or only non-text ele","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:39.464Z","tool":"save_changes","args":"{\"issue\":99001,\"content\":\"Scope: text underline (issue 99001) on desktop Chrome, Firefox and Safari, plus a mobile layout check; Ctrl means Cmd on macOS. Italic combined with underline is out of scope until italic ships.\\n\\n# Text properties\\n\\n## TC-1 \\\"Underline\\\" toggle: underlining a text and re","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:43.209Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"Underline is one property of the whole text element, set by an \\\"Underline\\\" toggle (tooltip \\\"Underline — Ctrl+U\\\") in the properties panel and by Ctrl+U / Cmd+U; the toggle is shown when a text, a shape with text or an arrow with a label is selected, or the Text t","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:45.007Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"Ctrl+U / Cmd+U toggles underline when a text, a shape with text or an arrow label is selected or a text is being edited, and then the browser's page source does not open; with nothing or only non-text elements selected it does nothing in the app, and touch devices h","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:46.611Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"The underline has the text color, its thickness and offset scale with the font size, each line of multi-line or wrapped text has its own underline as wide as that line's text, spaces are underlined and empty lines are not, and it may cross descenders.\",\"source\":\"App","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:48.159Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"With several texts selected and only some underlined, the \\\"Underline\\\" toggle shows a mixed state; one click underlines all of them and a second click removes underline from all; the last chosen underline value is the default for new text.\",\"source\":\"Approved answe","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:49.710Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"bound-text\",\"fact\":\"Underline works on text inside shapes, arrow labels and sticky note labels without changing wrapping or the shape's size, and a sticky note label shown smaller by auto-fit gets a matching smaller underline.\",\"source\":\"Approved answer 6 in the issue 99001 session, 2026-10","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:51.260Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"styles-and-history\",\"fact\":\"Copy and paste styles, Ctrl+C then Ctrl+V, Ctrl+D, Alt+drag and the library carry underline, and one underline toggle is undone by a single undo and restored by redo.\",\"source\":\"Approved answer 7 in the issue 99001 session, 2026-10-13 (PO answers relayed by maxxx","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:48:52.647Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"files-and-export\",\"fact\":\"Underline survives reload and saved .excalidraw files, appears in PNG and SVG exports and in live collaboration, and an older Excalidraw version opens such a file without error, showing the text without underline.\",\"source\":\"Approved answer 8 in the issue 99001 ses","outcome":"ok"}
